etry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c78" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=24;absoluteArcSize=1;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=4;fontFamily=Arial;strokeColor=#0070F2;fillColor=#EBF8FF;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="950" y="907" width="30" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c79" value='&lt;span style="font-size:12px;color:#1D2D3E"&gt;SAP&lt;/span&gt;' style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="988" y="905" width="60" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c80" value='&lt;span style="font-size:11px;color:#1D2D3E"&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt; Import every 8 min (Databricks) or dynamic tables, target_lag 10 min (Snowflake): new rows need no further step. &lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt; Schema change: republish share, ORD and CSN within one cycle. &lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt; BDC extracts the metadata, about 5 min. &lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt; Request access in Datasphere, approve in the BDC cockpit. &lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt; Install or reinstall the data product: manual, 30+ min for 137 tables, SAP side can lag by hours. &lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt; Remote tables read the shares live. &lt;b&gt;7&lt;/b&gt; SAP Analytics Cloud reads the Analytic Model.&lt;/span&gt;' style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="939" width="1730" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
